        <body>
            <div xml:id="d552">

                <pb facs="0449" n="437" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg437"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.515/75: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hibbard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-09-03T17:00:00-00:44">September 3,
                            1942—5 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 4—8:41 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>287. Department’s telegram no. 211, August 29, 9 [<hi rendition="#italic">4</hi>]
                    p.m. I have received today a note from the Liberian Secretary of State
                    confirming the agreement for acquisition of British current coin in Liberia in
                    exchange for United States current coin as contained in the Department’s
                    telegram No. 187, August 3, 8 p.m. The note is the same as the previous one
                    except that paragraph 3 has been omitted at my request in accordance with the
                    Treasury’s wishes. See my despatch no. 779 of August 29 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >25</hi>].<anchor n="75" xml:id="d552-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hibbard</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
